## Summary

I extended the business-day rule for the registration date to also skip public holidays, in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the single place this logic lives):

1. **Added the fixed public-holiday list** as a constant:
```java
private static final Set<LocalDate> PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
    LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 1),
    LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 26),
    LocalDate.of(2026, 4, 25),
    LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 25),
    LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 28));
```

2. **Updated `toBusinessDay`** so the roll-forward loop treats a listed holiday like a weekend, advancing one day at a time until it lands on a non-weekend, non-holiday day. This correctly handles chained cases too (e.g. 2026-12-25 Fri → skips Sat/Sun and the 12-28 Mon holiday → 2026-12-29):
```java
private LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
    while (isWeekend(date) || PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(date)) {
        date = date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
}
```

The adjusted date continues to flow through everything derived from it (membership number year segment, daily create-limit, etc.), since the adjustment happens at the single point where the registration date is set. My holiday set matches the test-side reference (`AcceptanceBase.HOLIDAYS`) exactly.

